Animation: find keys with plain comparisons, and match approximately once.

_find() compared every probed key with is_equal_approx() on the way down the
binary search. It now finds the first key after the time with plain comparisons,
then checks the keys either side of that position for an approximate match, the
only keys that can be one. Results are the same, except that a key within epsilon
of the time is always found as a match, where before it was only if a probe
landed on it.

Upstream: not proposed yet. Drop when an equivalent change is in the Godot we pin.

